(7223155, 1114091, 67258, '<td valign="top">Yes.  It is.  Extraordinary.  8 for the sheer weirdness - I would love to see just a tiny bit more detail in the shadow areas (OK, actually, I''m not entirely sure I am being truthful there...)</td>', 'Yes.  It is.  Extraordinary.  8 for the sheer weirdness - I would love to see just a tiny bit more detail in the shadow areas (OK, actually, I''m not entirely sure I am being truthful there...)', '2014-06-01 04:54:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(7223170, 1114791, 67258, '<td valign="top">Lovely and vibrant.</td>', 'Lovely and vibrant.', '2014-06-01 06:45:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(7223471, 1113964, 150277, '<td valign="top">Amazing color and sharpness.  Great image.</td>', 'Amazing color and sharpness.  Great image.', '2014-06-01 22:06:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(7223473, 1114787, 150277, '<td valign="top">I found this image very interesting.  The lighting makes the shot for me.  10.</td>', 'I found this image very interesting.  The lighting makes the shot for me.  10.', '2014-06-01 22:07:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(7223474, 1114748, 150277, '<td valign="top">How wonderful.  I cannot believe you let this little guy (or gal) so close to your camera.  But well done with the sharpness where it needed to be.</td>', 'How wonderful.  I cannot believe you let this little guy (or gal) so close to your camera.  But well done with the sharpness where it needed to be.', '2014-06-01 22:08:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(7223475, 1114549, 150277, '<td valign="top">Beautiful photo.  I love the bit of reflection and the black background.</td>', 'Beautiful photo.  I love the bit of reflection and the black background.', '2014-06-01 22:09:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(7223476, 1114459, 150277, '<td valign="top">What a fun image.  I like what you did the crayons in the shot, although that bit of emptiness in the upper left bothered me a bit.  I wonder what the shot would have looked with crayons all the way through the photo?  Still well done.</td>', 'What a fun image.  I like what you did the crayons in the shot, although that bit of emptiness in the upper left bothered me a bit.  I wonder what the shot would have looked with crayons all the way through the photo?  Still well done.', '2014-06-01 22:11:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(7223477, 1114730, 150277, '<td valign="top">There is a brightness to this photo that I adore.  I love the fence as the background too.</td>', 'There is a brightness to this photo that I adore.  I love the fence as the background too.', '2014-06-01 22:11:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(7223478, 1114709, 150277, '<td valign="top">Great lighting and simplicity.  My eye was drawn right to that ant.</td>', 'Great lighting and simplicity.  My eye was drawn right to that ant.', '2014-06-01 22:12:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(7223484, 1114811, 150277, '<td valign="top">I had to Google your title - so well done getting me to learn something.  I like the unique perspective you captured.  I thought this was a great capture of a macro, but the lack of any framing left me a bit dissatisfied.  It was like I wanted to understand how large (or small) this object was.  Were it not for your title I am not sure I would have known for sure it was a plant.  It looks perhaps like fur, or hairs on an animal.</td>', 'I had to Google your title - so well done getting me to learn something.  I like the unique perspective you captured.  I thought this was a great capture of a macro, but the lack of any framing left me a bit dissatisfied.  It was like I wanted to understand how large (or small) this object was.  Were it not for your title I am not sure I would have known for sure it was a plant.  It looks perhaps like fur, or hairs on an animal.', '2014-06-01 22:16:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(7223489, 1114673, 150277, '<td valign="top">I love the brightness to your colors, and nice timing to get such a sharp image of the lizard.  It felt like a bit too much emptiness in the upper left part of you photo.</td>', 'I love the brightness to your colors, and nice timing to get such a sharp image of the lizard.  It felt like a bit too much emptiness in the upper left part of you photo.', '2014-06-01 22:19:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(7223490, 1114702, 150277, '<td valign="top">Too cute.  Nice sharpness right where you wanted it, although that top part of the leaf, in the upper left, that is semi-sharp was a bit distracting.</td>', 'Too cute.  Nice sharpness right where you wanted it, although that top part of the leaf, in the upper left, that is semi-sharp was a bit distracting.', '2014-06-01 22:20:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(7223491, 1113994, 150277, '<td valign="top">Wonderful colors and sharpness.  The top left of you image was a bit dark for my tastes.</td>', 'Wonderful colors and sharpness.  The top left of you image was a bit dark for my tastes.', '2014-06-01 22:21:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(7223493, 1114737, 150277, '<td valign="top">Well done to capture a fly with such sharpness.</td>', 'Well done to capture a fly with such sharpness.', '2014-06-01 22:21:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(7223494, 1114693, 150277, '<td valign="top">I thought this was a lovely image.  Where did you find such an interesting number?  I noticed the few dusts spots - but not a lot you could do about that with minimal.  Well done.</td>', 'I thought this was a lovely image.  Where did you find such an interesting number?  I noticed the few dusts spots - but not a lot you could do about that with minimal.  Well done.', '2014-06-01 22:22:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(7223496, 1114757, 150277, '<td valign="top">Great capture of the caterpillar.  That one, darn blade of grass that blocked him just a bit was a little distracting.  But still, well done.</td>', 'Great capture of the caterpillar.  That one, darn blade of grass that blocked him just a bit was a little distracting.  But still, well done.', '2014-06-01 22:26:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(7223498, 1114030, 150277, '<td valign="top">Wonderful close-up.  That eye and beak have great sharpness.  I am not very good at understanding how portraits should be lit, so my preference could be way off base, but I wondered would the photo have been even stronger had his left side (closest to camera) had the highlights rather than the backside of his face?</td>', 'Wonderful close-up.  That eye and beak have great sharpness.  I am not very good at understanding how portraits should be lit, so my preference could be way off base, but I wondered would the photo have been even stronger had his left side (closest to camera) had the highlights rather than the backside of his face?', '2014-06-01 22:29:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(7223499, 1113669, 150277, '<td valign="top">What a great fine.  Well done with the sharpness.  I thought there may be a bit too much empty space on the right side of the image.</td>', 'What a great fine.  Well done with the sharpness.  I thought there may be a bit too much empty space on the right side of the image.', '2014-06-01 22:29:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(7223501, 1114470, 150277, '<td valign="top">What a crazy bug.  I have never seen anything like this.  The lighting sure showed him/her off, but I kept wishing the image was a bit closer up.</td>', 'What a crazy bug.  I have never seen anything like this.  The lighting sure showed him/her off, but I kept wishing the image was a bit closer up.', '2014-06-01 22:30:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(7224296, 1114663, 144746, '<td valign="top">Not bad</td>', 'Not bad', '2014-06-04 04:21:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(7224562, 1113857, 114225, '<td valign="top">I like this...not sure how "macro" it really is.</td>', 'I like this...not sure how "macro" it really is.', '2014-06-04 15:41:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(7224563, 1114188, 114225, '<td valign="top">Wonderful abstract.</td>', 'Wonderful abstract.', '2014-06-04 15:41:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(7224565, 1114822, 114225, '<td valign="top">Very neat shallow DOF effect.</td>', 'Very neat shallow DOF effect.', '2014-06-04 15:42:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(7224566, 1114811, 114225, '<td valign="top">Very cool.</td>', 'Very cool.', '2014-06-04 15:42:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(7224568, 1113788, 114225, '<td valign="top">I find myself really enjoying this.</td>', 'I find myself really enjoying this.', '2014-06-04 15:43:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(7224615, 1114750, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to bump up and to comment.<br/> <br/>The hankerchief, the stack of letters and the pocketwatch along with it''s warped reflection invokes the idea of passage of time. Perhaps these were old love letters or letters between friends and the inclusion of the clock and the aged look to the papers gives me the story that this was a long term relationship; one that lasted decades perhaps. I love this macro for it tells a story. Great job.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to bump up and to comment. The hankerchief, the stack of letters and the pocketwatch along with it''s warped reflection invokes the idea of passage of time. Perhaps these were old love letters or letters between friends and the inclusion of the clock and the aged look to the papers gives me the story that this was a long term relationship; one that lasted decades perhaps. I love this macro for it tells a story. Great job.', '2014-06-04 17:11:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(7224619, 1114748, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Now that is a serious close-up of a pig''s snout! A macro that is something different. Lighting and details are well done though it could use just a touch more of DOF to get sharper detail on the right nostril. Can''t help but thing of the rhyme, "This little piggy went to the market..."</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Now that is a serious close-up of a pig''s snout! A macro that is something different. Lighting and details are well done though it could use just a touch more of DOF to get sharper detail on the right nostril. Can''t help but thing of the rhyme, "This little piggy went to the market..."', '2014-06-04 17:14:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(7224626, 1114289, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment. <br/> <br/>Great job in catching the butterfly drinking nector AND with it''s wings open! Some great details of the flower as well and lovely hues both on the butterfly and the bokeh background. The only thing that I can suggest to make this composition even better is that if the back of the wings also were in sharp focus as the front - easier said than done I know for sometimes you just have to take the shot and hope when it comes to living creatures.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment.  Great job in catching the butterfly drinking nector AND with it''s wings open! Some great details of the flower as well and lovely hues both on the butterfly and the bokeh background. The only thing that I can suggest to make this composition even better is that if the back of the wings also were in sharp focus as the front - easier said than done I know for sometimes you just have to take the shot and hope when it comes to living creatures.', '2014-06-04 17:18:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(7224631, 1114731, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Wow! Now that is fantastic! Great details on this tiny ant from the texture on the legs to the mandibles! The green things...aphids?! Now that is impressive detail! I can even see the detail in the textured veins of the leaf! Love the light and the colors. Well done shot!</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Wow! Now that is fantastic! Great details on this tiny ant from the texture on the legs to the mandibles! The green things...aphids?! Now that is impressive detail! I can even see the detail in the textured veins of the leaf! Love the light and the colors. Well done shot!', '2014-06-04 17:22:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(7224634, 1114091, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Title is most appropriate for this capture. The cicada emerging from the darkness and so large in the frame takes on the frightening aspect of a monster from nightmares. Lighting and details are great on this creepy insect.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Title is most appropriate for this capture. The cicada emerging from the darkness and so large in the frame takes on the frightening aspect of a monster from nightmares. Lighting and details are great on this creepy insect.', '2014-06-04 17:24:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(7224636, 1113618, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>"Only their keys were found":-) I remember the great radio ads for this wine - and not a bad wine at that either:-) Great close-up on the cork showing the variation of color and texture in the wood as well as detail in the stamped label. The diagonal angle of the main subject was a good choice for it adds visual interest to the composition.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. "Only their keys were found":-) I remember the great radio ads for this wine - and not a bad wine at that either:-) Great close-up on the cork showing the variation of color and texture in the wood as well as detail in the stamped label. The diagonal angle of the main subject was a good choice for it adds visual interest to the composition.', '2014-06-04 17:28:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(7224656, 1114059, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Lighting is good, color is good and the details in the fabric and zipper are well done. The composition is what holds the photo back. Either angle or leading lines can help increase visual appeal as that generally straight on shots don''t hold the eye''s attention for very long. One suggestion I have to increase the visual appeal is to have the two sides of the zipper on top come out from the top left and top right corners....making the letter ''y'' which coincidentally would nicely correspond with the first letter of "Y" seen stamped into the metal zipper tab.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Lighting is good, color is good and the details in the fabric and zipper are well done. The composition is what holds the photo back. Either angle or leading lines can help increase visual appeal as that generally straight on shots don''t hold the eye''s attention for very long. One suggestion I have to increase the visual appeal is to have the two sides of the zipper on top come out from the top left and top right corners....making the letter ''y'' which coincidentally would nicely correspond with the first letter of "Y" seen stamped into the metal zipper tab.', '2014-06-04 18:27:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(7224658, 1114821, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Some great details in the stitching of the baseball and textures around it. Tis a shame that only a small portion in the forefront of the ball is in such sharp focus because more details of the full stitching and the textures of the ball could be accomplished. Since it is a still life you could set the camera on a tripod, set the aperture to a very high number to increase Depth of Field, and use a slower shutter speed to get the same lighting. That could get more sharper details all around rather than just the narrow spot here in this composition.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Some great details in the stitching of the baseball and textures around it. Tis a shame that only a small portion in the forefront of the ball is in such sharp focus because more details of the full stitching and the textures of the ball could be accomplished. Since it is a still life you could set the camera on a tripod, set the aperture to a very high number to increase Depth of Field, and use a slower shutter speed to get the same lighting. That could get more sharper details all around rather than just the narrow spot here in this composition.', '2014-06-04 18:33:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(7224660, 1114459, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Fantastic details on the jacket sleeve of the ''bittersweet'' crayon. I like the composition where you have the crayons angled on the diagonal for that adds visual interest with and interesting angle and leading lines that cut across the frame. The photo could do with just a touch more brightness and that could be easily achieved with more lighting on the subject. I wonder if it would be a bit better if there was greater Depth of field so that the crayons in back are in sharper focus as well but I am thinking you want to keep the main focus on the ''bittersweet'' crayon. A small suggestion that would increase the visual appeal even more is to include the tip of the bittersweet crayon in the top right corner for it would complete the leading line of the diagonal and put the full spotlight on your main subject by showing more of it.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Fantastic details on the jacket sleeve of the ''bittersweet'' crayon. I like the composition where you have the crayons angled on the diagonal for that adds visual interest with and interesting angle and leading lines that cut across the frame. The photo could do with just a touch more brightness and that could be easily achieved with more lighting on the subject. I wonder if it would be a bit better if there was greater Depth of field so that the crayons in back are in sharper focus as well but I am thinking you want to keep the main focus on the ''bittersweet'' crayon. A small suggestion that would increase the visual appeal even more is to include the tip of the bittersweet crayon in the top right corner for it would complete the leading line of the diagonal and put the full spotlight on your main subject by showing more of it.', '2014-06-04 18:41:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(7224701, 1114787, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Nice detail on the inner workings of the light bulb. I like that you lay your subject on a diagonal where the main subject fills the frame and travels from bottom left to top right. I think that the photo appeal would increase more if the full wire of the filiment was completely in the frame and that the bottom wall outline of the bulb was visible like it is on the top wall.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Nice detail on the inner workings of the light bulb. I like that you lay your subject on a diagonal where the main subject fills the frame and travels from bottom left to top right. I think that the photo appeal would increase more if the full wire of the filiment was completely in the frame and that the bottom wall outline of the bulb was visible like it is on the top wall.', '2014-06-04 19:57:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(7224703, 1114702, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment. <br/> <br/>What makes this shot is that ''expression'' on the spider that makes it look like it is frowning. Great details on the face, lighting is spot on, and the colors of the composition really pop. It is a great photo but I still wish that the legs were in sharper focus so that this little spider can be fully appreciated. Still, it is a great capture.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment.  What makes this shot is that ''expression'' on the spider that makes it look like it is frowning. Great details on the face, lighting is spot on, and the colors of the composition really pop. It is a great photo but I still wish that the legs were in sharper focus so that this little spider can be fully appreciated. Still, it is a great capture.', '2014-06-04 20:03:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(7224704, 1114340, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Very cool close-up of the typewriter dollar sign. Great light that shines on the metal bar so that your audience can see all the gritty details in the texture and the build-up of ink on the typeset that has occurred over years of use.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Very cool close-up of the typewriter dollar sign. Great light that shines on the metal bar so that your audience can see all the gritty details in the texture and the build-up of ink on the typeset that has occurred over years of use.', '2014-06-04 20:05:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(7224736, 1114737, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Great close-up of this Robber Fly. Wonderful sharp details, the colors are fabulous, and I like how you composed the leaf to be jutting out towards your audience. It is as if you are pushing forward your subject so that we can come in for a closer look. Nicely done.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Great close-up of this Robber Fly. Wonderful sharp details, the colors are fabulous, and I like how you composed the leaf to be jutting out towards your audience. It is as if you are pushing forward your subject so that we can come in for a closer look. Nicely done.', '2014-06-04 21:27:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(7224743, 1114661, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>They look like scooped out honeydew mellons in the shape of balls. Looked up galia and learned something new...wonder if the taste is vastly different or the same as honeydew mellon. Nice light and detail that shows off the how juicy sweet this natural treat is.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. They look like scooped out honeydew mellons in the shape of balls. Looked up galia and learned something new...wonder if the taste is vastly different or the same as honeydew mellon. Nice light and detail that shows off the how juicy sweet this natural treat is.', '2014-06-04 21:36:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(7224745, 1113669, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to bump up and to comment. <br/> <br/>Fantastic colors, great light and marvelous details from the snail to the thistle like flower! That snail is really hanging by a thread or rather a petal. Main subject pops very nicely off the bokeh backdrop. Well done.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to bump up and to comment.  Fantastic colors, great light and marvelous details from the snail to the thistle like flower! That snail is really hanging by a thread or rather a petal. Main subject pops very nicely off the bokeh backdrop. Well done.', '2014-06-04 21:40:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(7224766, 1114693, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Lighting and focus is great on this picture. You have some nice details visible in the texture of the number one. I think a vertical composition would have better complemented the vertical shape of your number one. While the shot is an excellent studio shot what is lacking in the composition is something that gives us a sense of scale. Something that we know is small paired with the number would give your audience a clue that this is a close-up shot as opposed to a very large number. Maybe a billard ball with the number one on it...something that gives a sense that the number is actually small.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Lighting and focus is great on this picture. You have some nice details visible in the texture of the number one. I think a vertical composition would have better complemented the vertical shape of your number one. While the shot is an excellent studio shot what is lacking in the composition is something that gives us a sense of scale. Something that we know is small paired with the number would give your audience a clue that this is a close-up shot as opposed to a very large number. Maybe a billard ball with the number one on it...something that gives a sense that the number is actually small.', '2014-06-04 22:37:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(7224770, 1114650, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment. <br/> <br/>Great timing to capture the dandelion seed taking flight - giving a sense of movement to the otherwise frozen in time capture. Lighting is nice and bright showing off the main subject of the bug and the flower. It looks as if the bug is hesitating - nervously watching the dandelion seed take off first. The main thing that would increase the visual appeal of this image even more is if you zoomed up to give your audience a more up close and personal look at this bug perched on the flower.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment.  Great timing to capture the dandelion seed taking flight - giving a sense of movement to the otherwise frozen in time capture. Lighting is nice and bright showing off the main subject of the bug and the flower. It looks as if the bug is hesitating - nervously watching the dandelion seed take off first. The main thing that would increase the visual appeal of this image even more is if you zoomed up to give your audience a more up close and personal look at this bug perched on the flower.', '2014-06-04 23:07:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(7224876, 1113587, 12611, '<td valign="top">I have these Carpenter style bees, and they infest the wood on one side of my garage. but they are slow, and I usually take out a few dozen with a badminton racket. I hate to do it, but it seems a better plan that poisoning my children, the earth, etc. When you knock them down they go from life to lifeless, hope they had a good run.8</td>', 'I have these Carpenter style bees, and they infest the wood on one side of my garage. but they are slow, and I usually take out a few dozen with a badminton racket. I hate to do it, but it seems a better plan that poisoning my children, the earth, etc. When you knock them down they go from life to lifeless, hope they had a good run.8', '2014-06-05 10:17:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(7224877, 1114673, 12611, '<td valign="top">What odd creatures there be.</td>', 'What odd creatures there be.', '2014-06-05 10:18:00.000000', NULL, 1),
