(7230779, 1114763, 129807, '<td valign="top">The colours are definitely what drew me to this when viewing the thumbs in your portfolio. You''ve managed to be bright and soft at the same time - well done. :)</td>', 'The colours are definitely what drew me to this when viewing the thumbs in your portfolio. You''ve managed to be bright and soft at the same time - well done. :)', '2014-06-19 03:23:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(7236038, 1114781, 50641, '<td valign="top">I love <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=643173" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">tomatillo husks</a> - nice interpretation here.  Did you process this after the challenge was over?  It has a lot of possibility.  Don''t worry about the sharpness comment. DPC has a sharpness fetish and macros usually need to be ~f/22 :P  The allure of your image is its waving in and out like a vertiginous stairwell.  FWIW you can sharpen more than once in minimal editing, should you choose to.</td>', 'I love tomatillo husks - nice interpretation here.  Did you process this after the challenge was over?  It has a lot of possibility.  Don''t worry about the sharpness comment. DPC has a sharpness fetish and macros usually need to be ~f/22 :P  The allure of your image is its waving in and out like a vertiginous stairwell.  FWIW you can sharpen more than once in minimal editing, should you choose to.', '2014-07-03 12:21:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(7236212, 1114781, 156466, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by skewsme:</b></div><hr/><i> I love <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=643173" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">tomatillo husks</a> - nice interpretation here.  Did you process this after the challenge was over?  It has a lot of possibility.  Don''t worry about the sharpness comment. DPC has a sharpness fetish and macros usually need to be ~f/22 :P  The allure of your image is its waving in and out like a vertiginous stairwell.  FWIW you can sharpen more than once in minimal editing, should you choose to. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for taking the time to comment.  Basic editing is a huge challenge for me.  With the team thing starting I never got to do anything significant with it, though I did a basic B&amp;W at first just to see where it would go.  Glad you got the idea of the intersection of 3 dimensions with a flat DOF.  I''ve got copies at a bunch of apertures and f/8 seemed to be the most interesting.  If I ever get an edit worth sharing I''ll post a link.</td>', 'Originally posted by skewsme: I love tomatillo husks - nice interpretation here.  Did you process this after the challenge was over?  It has a lot of possibility.  Don''t worry about the sharpness comment. DPC has a sharpness fetish and macros usually need to be ~f/22 :P  The allure of your image is its waving in and out like a vertiginous stairwell.  FWIW you can sharpen more than once in minimal editing, should you choose to.   Thanks for taking the time to comment.  Basic editing is a huge challenge for me.  With the team thing starting I never got to do anything significant with it, though I did a basic B&W at first just to see where it would go.  Glad you got the idea of the intersection of 3 dimensions with a flat DOF.  I''ve got copies at a bunch of apertures and f/8 seemed to be the most interesting.  If I ever get an edit worth sharing I''ll post a link.', '2014-07-03 20:15:23.000000', NULL, 0),
